{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## /rebar-debug FINAL REPORT — fix ready, landing via Gerrit\n\n**Problem (reproduced):** The deployed MCP container's `Config.Env` defines `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY` **twice** with conflicting values, so the effective (signing) value rests only on docker's unasserted last-wins ordering.\n\n**Proven root cause:** `mcp_run_new()` (infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:513) launches the MCP container with BOTH `--env-file \"$COMPOSE_DIR/.env\"` AND `-e REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY=/run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key`. `fetch-secrets.sh` was ALSO emitting `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY=<compose-dir>/rebar-bot-signing-key` into that shared `.env`. Unlike `docker compose` (which merges `environment:` over `env_file:` → one value), `docker run` appends BOTH the `--env-file` entry and the `-e` flag into `Config.Env` → the variable appears twice. Last-wins currently yields the op-cert path (correct), but nothing asserts it.\n\n**Why the `.env` copy is the dead/wrong duplicate:** the two services need DIFFERENT keys — the review-bot uses `/run/secrets/rebar-bot-signing-key` (compose `environment:`, docker-compose.yml:143) and the MCP container uses `/run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key` (compose:434 + the `-e` flag). A single shared `.env` cannot own both; each compose service already overrides it in its own `environment:` block, and `mcp_run_new` overrides via `-e`. The `.env` value was the review-bot HOST path, which does not exist inside the MCP container. There is no host-side consumer of the `.env` copy (only the two compose services + `mcp_run_new`, all of which override it).\n\n**Defect origin:** commit `2a0a4b1` (ticket `6964-40bb-46c9-48a7`, \"infra: add mcp blue-green autodeploy target\") added the `-e` alongside the pre-existing `--env-file`, creating the collision. The earlier `.env` emission (commit `2bbc3ae`, ticket neon-houndlike-ringworm) was correct at the time. Close class = `plan_defect`, `caused_by=6964-40bb-46c9-48a7`.\n\n**Safety (LAND, not escalate):** the op-cert value wins before AND after the fix → the signing identity is UNCHANGED. This is dead-override removal, not a key rotation. Review-bot is unaffected (keeps its compose `environment:` value + bind-mount).\n\n**Fix:** removed the `echo \"REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY=...\"` heredoc emission from `fetch-secrets.sh` so the variable is defined exactly once for the MCP container (the authoritative `-e` in `mcp_run_new`). The `signing_key_path` var is retained (still materializes the bot key file + logs). Comments updated to document the single-owner rule.\n\n**RED→GREEN proof:** new oracle `test_mcp_container_defines_signing_key_exactly_once` in tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py renders the real `.env` via `fetch-secrets.sh` (stubbed aws/curl) ∪ parses `mcp_run_new`'s `-e` flags, and asserts the composed env defines the key EXACTLY ONCE with effective value == op-cert path (anti-vacuity anchors included). Confirmed RED before the fix (defined twice), GREEN after; mutation check (re-adding the removed line) under an OS write-deny sandbox re-reddened it → test has teeth. Regression: full bluegreen suite (39 tests incl. the compose-parity test) + fetch-secrets consumer suites (test_mcp_client_pats, test_autodeploy_fetch_secrets, test_autodeploy_env_repr_security — 11 tests) all pass. `make lint` (ruff + shellcheck via check_shellcheck.py + zizmor), `make typecheck` (mypy 698 files) clean.\n\n**Sibling sweep:** computed overlap of `.env` keys vs `mcp_run_new` `-e` keys → EMPTY after fix. `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY` was the only duplicated variable; no other siblings.\n\n**Deploy / live verification:** per the DEPLOY NOTE, making this LIVE needs a deploy owned by the orchestrator (I did NOT run terraform apply). AC #2 (effective value stays op-cert in the running container) is best-determined from the config sources above and flagged for deploy-window confirmation.\n\n**Next:** committing with `rebar-ticket:` trailer + DCO sign-off and pushing to Gerrit; will Submit only on `LLM-Review +1` AND `Verified +1`, then close.\n\n(No key material printed anywhere — only container-side paths.)"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788066067139540385,"uuid":"c7e6250b-1005-4e5f-b9a8-365f3ea49f40"}